# What each guard weighs in the race job of ci.yml, in seconds under the race
# detector. .github/scripts/race_parts.py lays these out over the parts, the
# heaviest first, and sends every test not named here by the checksum of its
# name, counted at the "unlisted" weight.
#
# Taken on 2026-11-03 from eight parts of two runs, and on 2026-11-12 from the
# four parts of one more, each test at the longest time any of them took. The
# race job runs on whatever processor the runner is given, and the same part
# took 689 s on one and 1202 s on another, every test of it slower by the same
# factor. The longest time is the slowest processor's, so the parts are even
# where they are closest to the timeout. A time from a faster processor is
# scaled up by its part: on 2026-11-12 the listed tests of two parts on an AMD
# EPYC 9V74 took 1/1.20 and 1/1.15 of their weights.
# Listed: every test that took 10 s or more. "unlisted" is the mean of the rest.
#
# A test that is not here and takes 60 s or more fails its part with the line
# to add. A test that is here and no longer exists fails every part.
